# hc-patient-app — what Prettier does not format
#
# Two jobs. The first is the ordinary one: keep generated and vendored files out of scope. The
# second is the deliberate exclusion of `*.html`, which is a decision and not an oversight — read
# the second block before "fixing" it.
#
# This file exists so that a bare `npx prettier --check .` agrees with `npm run prettier:check`.
# Before it, the two disagreed: the npm scripts glob narrowly enough to miss `android/**/build/**`
# and the merged i18n bundles, so they passed by luck rather than by design.

# --- deliberate: Angular templates are hand-formatted ------------------------
#
# NO PRETTIER VERSION INDENTS INSIDE ANGULAR CONTROL FLOW. Measured 2026-09-08 against every
# release from 2.8.8 to 4.0.0-alpha.13: all of them flatten the contents of an `@if`/`@for` block
# to the parent's level, so
#
#     @if (item.notes) {                 becomes    @if (item.notes) {
#       <div class="hc-prose">…</div>               <div class="hc-prose">…</div>
#     }                                             }
#
# and a nested block loses its structure entirely. The 12 templates here are indented by hand and
# that is the readable form, so Prettier is pointed away from them rather than allowed to degrade
# them. This is not a stale pin waiting to be bumped: there is no newer version that fixes it, and
# raising the pin changes nothing about this file.
#
# `src/index.html` has no control flow and does conform — it is excluded with the rest so there is
# one rule about HTML here rather than two. `npm run lint` still checks templates through
# @angular-eslint/eslint-plugin-template; what is unenforced is whitespace, not correctness.
*.html

